n': 'Negative infinity compared to itself also results in NaN after subtraction, leading to false.'}]}, {'group': 'equals(double, double) - additional cases', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 0.0}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': -0.0}], 'expected': True, 'description': 'Positive zero and negative zero have a difference of 0.0, which is less than the tolerance, so they are considered equal.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 0.0}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 5e-324}], 'expected': True, 'description': 'The smallest positive sub‑normal double (Double.MIN_VALUE) differs from zero by ~4.9×10⁻³²⁴, well below the 1e‑12 tolerance.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 0.0}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 9.99999999999e-13}], 'expected': True, 'description': 'Difference (9.99999999999×10⁻¹³) is just under the tolerance (1e‑12), therefore the numbers are equal.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 0.0}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 1.000000000001e-12}], 'expected': False, 'description': 'Difference (1.000000000001×10⁻¹²) is just above the tolerance, so the method should return false.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 5e-13}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': -5e-13}], 'expected': False, 'description': "Numbers with opposite signs have an absolute difference of exactly 1e‑12 (the tolerance). Because the comparison uses '<' (strictly less), the result is false."}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 'NaN'}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 0.0}], 'expected': False, 'description': "Any comparison involving NaN yields false; subtraction results in NaN, and the '<' test fails."}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 'NaN'}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 'Infinity'}], 'expected': False, 'description': 'NaN compared with Infinity also returns false for the same reason as above.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 1.7976931348623157e+308}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 1.7976931348623157e+308}], 'expected': True, 'description': 'Two identical maximum‑value doubles have zero difference, which is less than the tolerance.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n1', 'value': 1.7976931348623157e+308}, {'parameter': 'n2', 'value': 1.7976931348623157e+308}], 'expected': True, 'description': 'Two maximum‑value doubles where the second operand is mathematically different but too small to affect the double representation (e.g., MAX_VALUE - 1e292). The subtraction underflows to 0.0, so the method reports equality.'}]}]
